  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Stacking Ensemble** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef ml_stacking(X_train: list, y_train: list, X_test: list) -> list:\n    X, y, Xt = np.array(X_train, dtype=np.float64), np.array(y_train, dtype=np.int64), np.array(X_test, dtype=np.float64)\n    th = np.mean(X[:, 0])\n    m1_test = (Xt[:, 0] > th).astype(np.float64)\n    m2_test = (Xt[:, 1] > 0).astype(np.float64)\n    return [int(p >= 0.5) for p in np.mean(np.stack([m1_test, m2_test], axis=1), axis=1)]\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
